    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0187" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/387</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-17">February 17, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department refers to its instruction
                    No. 722, dated December 30, 1927,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d41-f1"/> enclosing
                    copies of correspondence between the Department and the Board of Foreign
                    Missions of the Methodist Episcopal Church, New York City,<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d41-f2"/> in regard to claims for losses sustained by the Board in
                    China.</p>
                <p>In this connection there is transmitted herewith a copy of a letter, dated
                    January 25, 1930, from the Secretaries of the American Board of Commissioners
                    for Foreign Missions, of Boston, Massachusetts,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d41-f3"/>
                    with regard to the same subject, together with a copy of the Department’s reply
                        thereto.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d41-f4"/></p>
                <p>Any specific claims which may be brought to the attention of the American
                    diplomatic or consular officers in China on behalf of the American Board of
                    Commissioners for Foreign Missions should be transmitted to the Department for
                    approval and for instructions with regard to the prosecution of the claim.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
